From bad320d9c97e97803832aac535c1b517763fc186 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 07:23:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] CI: pin Database schema to ubuntu-24.04 before ubuntu-latest
 moves to 26.04

GitHub's notice on this job's runs on main: "The ubuntu-latest label will
migrate to Ubuntu 26 beginning October 19, 2026" (actions/runner-images
#14748). That image installs PostgreSQL 18 alone, under
/usr/lib/postgresql/18/bin, off PATH. db:check and db:fixtures build their
scratch cluster with the runner's own PostgreSQL, which
tools/db-check/src/cluster.ts looks for among versions 15 to 17, then on
PATH. On a 26.04 runner both would find nothing and fail every run, on main
and on every pull request.

24.04 keeps PostgreSQL 16, which every recorded run has used. Nothing else
in the workflow reads the runner's PostgreSQL. Moving this job, and adding
18 to the candidates, waits until both checks have passed on 18.

Found by a review of the db-check changes on claude/capability-decision-
writer, and kept apart from them so it can merge before 2026-10-19 on its
own.

npm run verify passes, ci-contract included (695 tests).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01N99CTZ1JH716U2E54THxmp
---
 .github/workflows/ci.yml | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/ci.yml b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
index 9610c95..bf3047d 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
@@ -80,7 +80,14 @@ jobs:
 
   database:
     name: Database schema
-    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    # Pinned, not ubuntu-latest: db:check and db:fixtures build their scratch cluster
+    # with the runner's own PostgreSQL, found by tools/db-check/src/cluster.ts among
+    # versions 15 to 17. ubuntu-latest moves to Ubuntu 26.04 from 2026-10-19 (GitHub's
+    # notice on this job), whose image installs PostgreSQL 18 alone, off PATH, so both
+    # would find nothing and fail every run. 24.04 has PostgreSQL 16, which every
+    # recorded run has used. Move this, and add 18 to the candidates, only once both
+    # have passed on 18.
+    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04
     steps:
       - uses: actions/checkout@v4
       - uses: actions/setup-node@v4
-- 
